{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1540818-how-would-you-go-about-making-a-halberd-wielder","id":1540818,"title":"How would you go about making a Halberd wielder?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-20T19:52:11-07:00","id":1540818,"title":"How would you go about making a Halberd wielder?","content":"Hello, how would you go about making a halberd using character? I have been watching some HEMA, and Kenjutsu uses for the Halberd so it got me wondering?<br /> -I will just be using a basic artifact halberd instead of concerning myself with invocations. <br /> <br /> Using the Grimscythe stat block which makes more sense than a dire lance. <br /> Stats: Lethal, Melee, Piercing, Reaching, Two-Handed<br /> Heavy Artifact: +1 Accuracy, +14 Damage, +0 Defense, 5 overwhelming<br /> (Notes: I would likely add disarming, as they are quite good at that. But that isn't necessary.)<br /> <br /> So we have a lot of damage, and lower defense so perhaps using it with a lot of area attacks such as Heaven Sword Flash at higher essence, and maybe some counterattack or clashing charms such as Fervent Blow? In fact Fervent Blow seems perfect. Other than that I would say some good armor, just in case but likely not that many of the Defend Other charms such as War Lion Stance?<br /> <br /> Non-combat skills?<br /> Probably some war charms, as I would think of a halberd user as someone with war experience as swords are better for single combat but a halberd is closer to a spear which is the epitomy of real infantry weapons? This also implies he is not going to be a navy guy so no sail, and a halberd is not a cavalry weapon either so low or no ride. Resistance &amp; Athletics make sense, especially with all the marching?<br /> <br /> Anyone have any further ideas or disagree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T23:24:05-07:00","id":1541221,"title":"","content":"Whatever trait it is to have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=riVyHnMtf-0\" target=\"_blank\">your theme song play</a> as you beat the living hell out of your opponents is a must.<br /> <br /> The down to earth traits of a halberd are going to be less important as an Artifact weapon than the legendary Evocations of said weapon, so having a few more tags like Chopping probably isn't going to break the bank if it makes sense. It is a bare minimum rating 3 item, after all. Beyond that, whatever personal style of combat you envisioned your character being good at is the order of the day, because you don't really need to optimize Solar Charms so much, especially if you start cranking up the rating of your Sky Scorcher and it now has a bunch of potential tie-ins with whatever Solar Charms you want it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T02:36:02-07:00","id":1543576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1540818-how-would-you-go-about-making-a-halberd-wielder#post1540818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using the Grimscythe stat block which makes more sense than a dire lance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Poleaxe/Halberd is a Heavy Melee <i>Mortal</i> Weapon (Ex3 585), so in-game stats exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Stats: Lethal, Melee, Chopping, Reaching, Two-Handed Mortal Weapon : +0 Accuracy, +11 Damage, -1 Defense, 1 Overwhelming. Heavy Artifact: +1 Accuracy, +14 Damage, +0 Defense, 5 Overwhelming.</pre> </div>But whether you tag it with Chopping, Piercing, or even Grappling is up to you, I guess.<br /> <br /> Halberds were all round weapons designed for cutting, thrusting, or dismounting opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 10-11-2024, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T16:36:36-08:00","id":1545542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1540818-how-would-you-go-about-making-a-halberd-wielder?p=1543576#post1543576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Poleaxe/Halberd is a Heavy Melee <i>Mortal</i> Weapon (Ex3 585), so in-game stats exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, Sun's Brush (Arms/Chosen 44) is described as a naginata, but statted as a Grimcleaver, a Medium Melee Artifact Weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}